-- Old Age Security Act, PART II, sections 16 to 18.2: consideration of an application and notice of the decision,
-- when payment is made, the adjustment when the income shown turns out wrong, and ceasing or cancelling the
-- supplement. Piece oa2.
--
-- What the Minister may or must do is a BOOLEAN rule over the facts the section names, as in sections 11 and 15.
-- The prescribed time limits of ss 18.2(1) and (2) are Regulations 26.1 (piece oa3) and enter as inputs named for
-- them.

§ `Part II -- Monthly Guaranteed Income Supplement`

§§ `Payment of supplement, sections 16 and 17`

-- (1) "The Minister shall, without delay after receiving an application for payment of a supplement under subsection
-- 11(2) or after waiving the requirement for an application for payment of a supplement under subsection 11(3.1) or
-- (4), as the case may be, consider whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement, and may approve
-- payment of a supplement and fix its amount, or may determine that no supplement may be paid."
-- src:487 | 16 (1) The Minister shall, without delay after receiving an application for payment of a supplement under subsection 11(2) or after waiving the requirement for an application for payment of a supplement under subsection 11(3.1) or (4), as the case may be, consider whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement, and may approve payment of a supplement and fix its amount, or may determine that no supplement may be paid.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 16(1) (src:487)
GIVEN `the Minister has received an application for payment of a supplement under subsection 11(2)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(3.1) or (4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(1): the Minister must consider without delay whether the applicant is entitled to be paid a supplement` `the Minister has received an application for payment of a supplement under subsection 11(2)` `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(3.1) or (4)` MEANS
    `the Minister has received an application for payment of a supplement under subsection 11(2)` OR `the Minister has waived the requirement for an application under subsection 11(3.1) or (4)`

-- (2) "Where particulars of the basis on which the amount of any supplement that may be paid to an applicant was
-- fixed by the Minister are requested by the applicant or where the Minister determines that no supplement may be
-- paid to the applicant, the Minister shall forthwith in writing notify the applicant of the basis on which that
-- amount was fixed or of the decision that no supplement may be paid to the applicant and the Minister's reasons
-- therefor, as the case may be."
-- src:489 | (2) Where particulars of the basis on which the amount of any supplement that may be paid to an applicant was fixed by the Minister are requested by the applicant or where the Minister determines that no supplement may be paid to the applicant, the Minister shall forthwith in writing notify the applicant of the basis on which that amount was fixed or of the decision that no supplement may be paid to the applicant and the Minister’s reasons therefor, as the case may be.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 16(2) basis requested (src:489)
GIVEN `the applicant has requested particulars of the basis on which the amount of the supplement was fixed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the basis on which the amount was fixed` `the applicant has requested particulars of the basis on which the amount of the supplement was fixed` MEANS
    `the applicant has requested particulars of the basis on which the amount of the supplement was fixed`

-- src:489 | (2) Where particulars of the basis on which the amount of any supplement that may be paid to an applicant was fixed by the Minister are requested by the applicant or where the Minister determines that no supplement may be paid to the applicant, the Minister shall forthwith in writing notify the applicant of the basis on which that amount was fixed or of the decision that no supplement may be paid to the applicant and the Minister’s reasons therefor, as the case may be.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 16(2) no supplement (src:489)
GIVEN `the Minister has determined that no supplement may be paid to the applicant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 16(2): the Minister must forthwith notify the applicant in writing of the decision that no supplement may be paid and the Minister's reasons` `the Minister has determined that no supplement may be paid to the applicant` MEANS
    `the Minister has determined that no supplement may be paid to the applicant`

-- 17 "Payment of a supplement for any month shall be made in arrears at the end of the month, except that where
-- payment of a supplement in respect of months in any payment period is approved after the end of the month for which
-- the first payment of the supplement may be made, payments of the supplement for the month in which payment of the
-- supplement is approved and for months before that month may be made at the end of that month or at the end of the
-- month immediately after that month."
DECLARE `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made` HAS
    `the earliest day` IS A DATE
    `the latest day` IS A DATE

-- src:491 | 17 Payment of a supplement for any month shall be made in arrears at the end of the month, except that where payment of a supplement in respect of months in any payment period is approved after the end of the month for which the first payment of the supplement may be made, payments of the supplement for the month in which payment of the supplement is approved and for months before that month may be made at the end of that month or at the end of the month immediately after that month.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 17 (src:491)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the month for which the first payment of the supplement may be made` IS A DATE
      `the day on which payment of the supplement is approved` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made`
`s 17: the end-of-month days on which payment for the month may be made` month `the month for which the first payment of the supplement may be made` `the day on which payment of the supplement is approved` MEANS
    IF     `the day on which payment of the supplement is approved` GREATER THAN `the last day of the month containing` `the month for which the first payment of the supplement may be made`
       AND `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` `the day on which payment of the supplement is approved`
    THEN `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made` OF
             (`the last day of the month containing` `the day on which payment of the supplement is approved`),
             (`the last day of the month containing` (`the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the day on which payment of the supplement is approved`))
    ELSE `s 17: End-of-month days on which payment may be made` OF
             (`the last day of the month containing` month),
             (`the last day of the month containing` month)

§§ `Adjustment of payments, section 18`

-- 18 "Where it is determined that the income for a base calendar year (in this section referred to as the 'actual
-- income') of an applicant for a supplement does not accord with the income of the applicant (in this section
-- referred to as the 'shown income') calculated on the basis of a statement or an estimate made under section 14,
-- the following adjustments shall be made".
-- (a) "if the actual income exceeds the shown income, any amount by which the supplement paid to the applicant for
-- months in the payment period exceeds the supplement that would have been paid to the applicant for those months if
-- the shown income had been equal to the actual income shall be deducted and retained out of any subsequent payments
-- of supplement or pension made to the applicant, in any manner that may be prescribed" (the manner is prescribed
-- by the Regulations, out of range: section 18 prescribed manner (piece oa3); it changes how, not how much).
-- src:495 | 18 Where it is determined that the income for a base calendar year (in this section referred to as the “actual income”) of an applicant for a supplement does not accord with the income of the applicant (in this section referred to as the “shown income”) calculated on the basis of a statement or an estimate made under section 14, the following adjustments shall be made:
-- src:496 | (a) if the actual income exceeds the shown income, any amount by which the supplement paid to the applicant for months in the payment period exceeds the supplement that would have been paid to the applicant for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income shall be deducted and retained out of any subsequent payments of supplement or pension made to the applicant, in any manner that may be prescribed; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18(a) (src:495-496)
GIVEN `the actual income` IS A NUMBER
      `the shown income` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement paid to the applicant for months in the payment period` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(a): the amount to be deducted and retained out of subsequent payments of supplement or pension` `the actual income` `the shown income` `the supplement paid to the applicant for months in the payment period` `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income` MEANS
    IF `the actual income` GREATER THAN `the shown income`
    THEN max 0 (`the supplement paid to the applicant for months in the payment period` MINUS `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income`)
    ELSE 0

-- (b) "if the shown income exceeds the actual income, there shall be paid to the applicant any amount by which the
-- supplement that would have been paid to the applicant for months in the payment period if the actual income had been
-- equal to the shown income exceeds the supplement paid to the applicant for those months."
-- As written, "the supplement that would have been paid [...] if the actual income had been equal to the shown income"
-- is the supplement that was paid, because the supplement paid was calculated on the shown income; the difference is
-- nothing, and paragraph (b) would never pay anything (fork F-18-1, finding). The mirror of (a) is evidently meant:
-- the supplement that would have been paid if the SHOWN income had been equal to the ACTUAL income. Both are encoded;
-- the seat uses the second and says so.
-- src:497 | (b) if the shown income exceeds the actual income, there shall be paid to the applicant any amount by which the supplement that would have been paid to the applicant for months in the payment period if the actual income had been equal to the shown income exceeds the supplement paid to the applicant for those months.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18(b) as written (src:497)
GIVEN `the actual income` IS A NUMBER
      `the shown income` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement paid to the applicant for those months` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the actual income had been equal to the shown income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as it is written` `the actual income` `the shown income` `the supplement paid to the applicant for those months` `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the actual income had been equal to the shown income` MEANS
    IF `the shown income` GREATER THAN `the actual income`
    THEN max 0 (`the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the actual income had been equal to the shown income` MINUS `the supplement paid to the applicant for those months`)
    ELSE 0

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18(b) (src:497)
GIVEN `the actual income` IS A NUMBER
      `the shown income` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement paid to the applicant for those months` IS A NUMBER
      `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 18(b): the amount to be paid to the applicant, read as the mirror of paragraph (a)` `the actual income` `the shown income` `the supplement paid to the applicant for those months` `the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income` MEANS
    IF `the shown income` GREATER THAN `the actual income`
    THEN max 0 (`the supplement that would have been paid for those months if the shown income had been equal to the actual income` MINUS `the supplement paid to the applicant for those months`)
    ELSE 0

§§ `Cessation of payment, section 18.1`

-- 18.1 "If a pensioner makes a request to the Minister in writing that their supplement cease to be payable, it shall
-- cease to be payable on the last day of the month in which the Minister approves the request and shall not resume
-- until the later of the month after the month in which the Minister receives a new application for the supplement
-- and the month chosen by the pensioner in the application."
-- src:501 | 18.1 If a pensioner makes a request to the Minister in writing that their supplement cease to be payable, it shall cease to be payable on the last day of the month in which the Minister approves the request and shall not resume until the later of the month after the month in which the Minister receives a new application for the supplement and the month chosen by the pensioner in the application.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18.1 last day (src:501)
GIVEN `the month in which the Minister approves the request` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 18.1: the last day of the month on which the supplement ceases to be payable` `the month in which the Minister approves the request` MEANS
    `the last day of the month containing` `the month in which the Minister approves the request`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18.1 "shall not resume until the later of" (src:501)
GIVEN `the month in which the Minister receives a new application for the supplement` IS A DATE
      `the month chosen by the pensioner in the application` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 18.1: the first month in which the supplement may resume` `the month in which the Minister receives a new application for the supplement` `the month chosen by the pensioner in the application` MEANS
    IF afterReceipt GREATER THAN chosen THEN afterReceipt ELSE chosen
    WHERE
        afterReceipt MEANS `the first day of the month that is` 1 `months after the month containing` `the month in which the Minister receives a new application for the supplement`
        chosen MEANS `the first day of the month containing` `the month chosen by the pensioner in the application`

@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18.1 (src:501)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `the pensioner has made a request to the Minister in writing that their supplement cease to be payable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the month in which the Minister approves the request` IS A DATE
      `the first month in which the supplement may resume (any date if no new application)` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18.1: the supplement is payable for the month in spite of the request` month `the pensioner has made a request to the Minister in writing that their supplement cease to be payable` `the month in which the Minister approves the request` `the first month in which the supplement may resume (any date if no new application)` MEANS
        NOT `the pensioner has made a request to the Minister in writing that their supplement cease to be payable`
    OR `the first day of the month containing` month AT MOST `the first day of the month containing` `the month in which the Minister approves the request`
    OR CONSIDER `the first month in which the supplement may resume (any date if no new application)`
       WHEN JUST resumes THEN `the first day of the month containing` month AT LEAST `the first day of the month containing` resumes
       WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE

§§ `Cancellation of payment, section 18.2`

-- 18.2(1) "A pensioner may, in the prescribed manner and within the prescribed time after payment of a supplement
-- has commenced, request cancellation of that supplement." Both the manner and the time are prescribed (Regulations
-- s 26.1, piece oa3); the time is an input and the manner is a fact the caller states.
-- src:505 | 18.2 (1) A pensioner may, in the prescribed manner and within the prescribed time after payment of a supplement has commenced, request cancellation of that supplement.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18.2(1) (src:505)
GIVEN `the request is made in the prescribed manner` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Regulations section 26.1 (piece oa3)
      `the day on which payment of the supplement commenced` IS A DATE
      `the prescribed time after payment of the supplement has commenced` IS A `Time limit`     -- out of range: Regulations section 26.1 (piece oa3)
      `the day on which the request is made` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18.2(1): the pensioner may request cancellation of the supplement` `the request is made in the prescribed manner` `the day on which payment of the supplement commenced` `the prescribed time after payment of the supplement has commenced` `the day on which the request is made` MEANS
        `the request is made in the prescribed manner`
    AND `the day on which the request is made` AT LEAST `the day on which payment of the supplement commenced`
    AND `the day on which the request is made` AT MOST `the day that is` `the prescribed time after payment of the supplement has commenced` `after` `the day on which payment of the supplement commenced`

-- (2) "If the request is granted and the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the
-- prescribed time, (a) the application for that supplement is deemed never to have been made; and (b) the supplement is
-- deemed for the purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period in question."
-- src:507 | (2) If the request is granted and the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time,
-- src:508 | (a) the application for that supplement is deemed never to have been made; and
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18.2(2)(a) (src:507-508)
GIVEN `the request is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Regulations section 26.1 (piece oa3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18.2(2)(a): the application for the supplement is deemed never to have been made` `the request is granted` `the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time` MEANS
    `the request is granted` AND `the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time`

-- src:507 | (2) If the request is granted and the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time,
-- src:508 | (a) the application for that supplement is deemed never to have been made; and
-- src:509 | (b) the supplement is deemed for the purposes of this Act not to have been payable during the period in question.
@ref R.S.C., 1985, c. O-9, s 18.2(2)(b) (src:507-509)
GIVEN `the request is granted` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time` IS A BOOLEAN     -- out of range: Regulations section 26.1 (piece oa3)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 18.2(2)(b): the supplement is deemed not to have been payable during the period in question` `the request is granted` `the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time` MEANS
    `the request is granted` AND `the amount of any supplement and related allowance is repaid within the prescribed time`
